se O-2 molecule.).\n- **Dissociation barrier:** The lowest activation energy for dissociation is about 0.20 eV (Possible pathways for the dissociation Of O-2 are explored, and the lowest activation energy is calculated to be ca. 0.20 eV.).\n- **Strain effect:** Expansive strain parallel to the surface strengthens binding of both atomic and molecular oxygen and lowers the dissociation transition-state energy (Expansive strain parallel to the surface plane is shown to enhance the binding of atomic and molecular oxygen on the surface as well as to decrease the transition state energy of O-2 dissociation.).\n- **Cross-check:** A later arXiv study using different methods reports a fcc-site O binding energy of -5.000 eV, with hcp at -4.905 eV (Oxygen (O*) fcc -5.000 hcp -4.905). That value is about 0.7 eV more negative than the 2001 figure, so the two numbers should not be compared directly without checking the reference state and functional used."],"durationSeconds":7.7837565600000085,"searchCount":1},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01RKa7EaZVwj5sS6kMxt4sYq","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
