e O atom: -4.3 eV (PW91, Xu & Mavrikakis, Surf. Sci. 494 (2001) 131, abstract) and -5.000 eV (fcc) / -4.905 eV (hcp) (PBE, arXiv:2505.12914). Our -4.84 eV and the fcc-over-hcp ordering fall within that spread. Premise: no direct experimental value exists for an isolated O atom reference, so this is a PBE-level (0 K, no ZPE) quantity. MLIP caveat: the O atom energy is the model's fitted per-element E0, not a spin-polarized triplet PBE atom calculation. That reference was validated indirectly: the Cu cohesive energy using the same type of atom reference is 3.501 eV vs 3.49 exp, and the O2 binding energy (6.29 eV) is PBE-like. Uncertainty +-0.3 eV covers MLIP-vs-PBE error including the atom-reference E0, the spread in published GGA values, and the size and coverage effects (<0.07 eV). It does NOT cover GGA functional error: PBE overbinds O2 by about 1 eV, so the gas-atom reference energy is itself functional-dependent. Combining our E_ads vs 1/2 O2 (-1.69 eV) with the experimental O2 De (5.21 eV) gives about -4.30 eV, an experiment-anchored estimate.\"}\nEOF\n./board post property_result @/work/scripts/result.json --parent 848d14e2-d4d7-4b1f-8ee4-db8cda29ab05"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":637,"cache_read_input_tokens":31276,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":637,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":20,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e8134b61-5a82-4eb5-8ce2-5d1136f1766d","uuid":"9e5d9c4d-7896-48cc-9ee4-65dc901f42e2","timestamp":"2026-11-01T02:54:01.162Z","request_id":"req_011CgbTDE2fd3r86FTEGDQXo","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01LyPQNULHnPjHpzmTaFf15t":{"command":"cd /work && cat > /work/scripts/result.json <<'EOF'\n{\"candidate\": \"O on Cu(111)\", \"family\": \"metal su