{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgbTEjErh4YRqdc7dEyMP","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Atomic oxygen binds most strongly at the **fcc hollow site** on Cu(111), with an adsorption energy of **E_ads = −4.84 ± 0.3 eV** relative to an isolated O atom. This is a 0 K, PBE-level number with no zero-point energy. It is posted on the board as `property_result` 33bffa19.\n\n**Premise check.** The quantity is well-defined at 0 K for an ordinary DFT-type calculation. Nobody measures it directly against a free O atom, so there is no experimental value to compare with. Since this is a static energy, no molecular dynamics was needed.\n\nThe main weak point is the isolated O atom. In this model (MACE-MPA-0 medium) a lone atom just gets a fixed energy per element. It is not a real calculation of a spin-polarised O atom. I tested that reference indirectly, below, rather than rejecting the task.\n\n**How it was run.**\n- I first relaxed the Cu lattice constant: 3.640 Å.\n- The surface was a 3×3, 4-layer Cu slab with the bottom 2 layers fixed, giving 1/9 monolayer coverage. Geometry was relaxed until forces were below 0.01 eV/Å.\n- I tried four sites:\n\n| Site | E_ads (eV) |\n|---|---|\n| fcc hollow | **−4.837** |\n| hcp hollow | −4.783 |\n| top | −3.08 |\n| bridge | relaxes into fcc |\n\n- Relative to ½ O₂ instead of the atom, the fcc value is −1.69 eV.\n- Changing the slab size moved the fcc value by at most 0.07 eV. Larger slabs (3×3×6 and 4×4×5) agree with the result to within 0.01 eV. The smallest slab (2×2, 1/4 coverage) gives −4.90 eV.\n\n**Validation with the same setup.**\n\n| Quantity | This model | Known value |\n|---|---|---|\n| Cu lattice constant | 3.640 Å | 3.615 Å (experiment) |\n| Cu cohesive energy | 3.501 eV/atom | 3.49 eV |\n| O₂ bond length | 1.235 Å | 1.208 Å |\n| O₂ binding energy | 6.29 eV | 5.21 eV (experiment) |\n\n- The Cu cohesive energy uses the same kind of free-atom reference as the main result, so its close match is the most relevant test.\n- PBE is known to overbind O₂, and the model's 6.29 eV shows that same PBE-like overbinding.\n- Published DFT values for this site range from about −4.3 eV ([Xu & Mavrikakis 2001](https://data.zhenzhi.com/details/1/867115130)) to −5.000 eV ([arXiv:2505.12914](https://www.arxiv.org/pdf/2505.12914)). That paper also finds fcc favoured over hcp, by 0.095 eV; I get 0.05 eV. My number falls inside that range.\n\n**Uncertainty.** The ±0.3 eV covers:\n- error of the model relative to PBE, including the free-atom reference;\n- the spread between published DFT values;\n- slab-size and coverage effects.\n\nIt does **not** cover the error built into PBE itself. Because PBE overbinds O₂ by about 1 eV, the energy of a free O atom depends on the method. If I combine my −1.69 eV (relative to ½ O₂) with the experimental O₂ binding energy, the estimate shifts to about **−4.3 eV**. The board note records this.\n\n**On the board.**\n- The `candidate`, fulfilling need #0.\n- The `property_result` with full method details and no flags.\n- A `literature_anchor` check marked \"pass\". My first try at that check used a type name the board doesn't accept, so nothing was posted from it.\n\nThe calibration file (melting points and similar) has nothing on adsorption, so I didn't use it.\n\nSources:\n- [arXiv:2505.12914](https://www.arxiv.org/pdf/2505.12914)\n- [Xu & Mavrikakis, Surf. Sci. 2001 (abstract)](https://data.zhenzhi.com/details/1/867115130)\n- [Structural and electronic properties of atomic O on Cu(111)](https://bvbvf1.bib-bvb.de/vufind/PrimoRecord/cdi_chongqing_primary_44769476)\n- [Tohoku ACCMS poster](https://accms.mobility.niche.tohoku.ac.jp/ACCMS-11/POSTER/P-46_a11_6122919.pdf) — not used: it gives −6.37 eV with an unclear reference."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":436,"cache_read_input_tokens":33989,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":436,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e8134b61-5a82-4eb5-8ce2-5d1136f1766d","uuid":"33ba3bf4-d472-403c-b4ad-9ef7c5e4085b","timestamp":"2026-11-01T02:54:22.503Z","request_id":"req_011CgbTEitXczGt2LZ3vvSVa"}
